    "senderName": "NWS San Diego CA",
    "headline": "High Wind Warning issued October 15 at 1:39PM PDT until October 17 at 8:00PM PDT by NWS San Diego CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...For eastern portions of the valleys, northeast to east winds\n20 to 30 mph with gusts 45 to 55 mph expected, locally higher up to\n70 mph near mountain foothills. For the western valleys, more\nlocalized wind gusts 35 to 45 mph. Strongest and most widespread\nwinds will be on Friday.\n\n* WHERE...San Diego County Valleys.\n\n* WHEN...From 8 PM this evening to 8 PM PDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Damaging winds will blow down trees and power lines.\nWidespread power outages are expected. Travel will be difficult for\nhigh profile vehicles.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...Winds will become easterly on Saturday.",
    "instruction": "People are urged to secure loose objects that could be blown around\nor damaged by the wind.",
